<title>UK: UK considers tax credit for low-paid workers.</title>
<headline>UK considers tax credit for low-paid workers.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK Chancellor Gordon Brown said on Wednesday that the UK would consider the advantages of introducing an in-work tax credit for low-paid workers.</p>
<p>&quot;It would draw on the experience of the American earned income tax credit, which helps reduce in-work poverty and now helps 19 million lower paid workers,&quot; Brown told Parliament.</p>
<p>He said he had asked Martin Taylor, chief executive of Barclays Plc and leader of the welfare-to-work shceme, to undertake the review. --London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
